      "prompt": "Solve $2(3x + 6) = 6x + 12$. State whether the equation has one solution, no solution, or infinitely many solutions.",
      "answer": "Infinitely many solutions (identity)",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "Distribute on the left: $6x + 12 = 6x + 12$.",
          "Subtract $6x$ from both sides: $12 = 12$.",
          "Because $12 = 12$ is always true, every value of $x$ works, so there are infinitely many solutions."
